### triage-flow — AiAgent state example (stateType 6, experimental)
### "classifying" runs triage-agent on entry; the model picks one of the state's rule-less automatic
### transitions (is-question / is-fraud). classify-failed is the required fallback, too-many is taken
### once the state was entered more than policy.maxEntries (2) times.
### With the "local" provider the decision resolves to the first candidate (is-question -> answered).
### Publish Agents/ and Workflows/ first (wf sync publishes agents before workflows).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4201
@apiVersion = 1
@domain = core
@workflow = triage-flow
@instanceId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Start an instance; the agent runs when the instance enters "classifying"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/start?sync=true
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Where is my card?"
}

### State (expected: answered)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{instanceId}}/functions/state

### Instance data: the agent output lands at $.triage, with the $agent run summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{instanceId}}/functions/data

### Agent runs, newest first, with their decision (?state=, ?skip=, ?take= up to 100)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{instanceId}}/functions/agent-runs

### Ask again: re-enters "classifying" (the third entry exceeds maxEntries and goes to "exhausted")
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{instanceId}}/transitions/ask-again?sync=true
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "And when will the new one arrive?"
}

### Close
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v{{apiVersion}}/{{domain}}/workflows/{{workflow}}/instances/{{instanceId}}/transitions/close?sync=true
Content-Type: application/json

{}
